//www.youtube.com/watch?v=SCac9sicitA", "video_id": "SCac9sicitA", "duration_s": 599, "thumb": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/SCac9sicitA/mqdefault.jpg", "hosts": ["Adam Aizer", "Jamey Eisenberg"], "summary": "A 10-minute early waiver episode on Jamey's 50th birthday. **Omar Cooper Jr.** is the headliner, though Adam worries about Adonai Mitchell's return and Garrett Wilson. **DeMario Douglas** is a low-FAB add, **Hunter Henry** is \"the easy one\" at TE, with **Mayer** behind him. For QBs, **Murray** and **Rodgers** are the Week 7 starters (slight nod Rodgers), and **McCarthy** is a must-add in 2QB/Superflex. RBs got a flat \"No,\" with Tracy, Miller and Knight as the deep options. The **Vikings** are the #1 DST. Every stat checked out against Sleeper. For you, Poncho: the MAIN wire has Murray, Henry, Mayer, Cooper, Douglas and three of the four DSTs, which helps with Allen's bye and Andrews's slump. Freddy has Henry on his DYNASTY bench and Rodgers on his MAIN bench.", "segments": [{"ts": "00:00\u201300:50", "title": "00:00\u201300:50 \u00b7 Intro \u00b7 Jamey: \"one of those weeks where it's not great\u2026 thankfully [no] big injury replacements.\" Croskey-Merritt (\"Jory Kimmer\") won't play MNF vs SF, so Rachaad White / Austin Ekeler are in range. \"A good week to find a backup quarterback or maybe a long-term answer quarterback.\""}, {"ts": "00:50\u201302:00", "title": "00:50\u201302:00 \u00b7 Omar Cooper Jr. \u00b7 Jamey's headliner. Rookie WR class rant (Bernard, Tate, Stribling). Adam's pushback: Adonai Mitchell's return + Garrett Wilson (the \"Christian Gonzalez shut him down\" reply is probably Jamey)"}, {"ts": "02:00\u201303:15", "title": "02:00\u201303:15 \u00b7 Wide receivers \u00b7 DeMario Douglas, Kendrick Bourne, Khalil Shakir, KC Concepcion, Ja'Kobi Lane, Jordan Tyson (IR stash)."}, {"ts": "03:15\u201304:30", "title": "03:15\u201304:30 \u00b7 Running backs \u00b7 \"Any good running backs to pick up this week?\" \"No.\" Then: Kendre Miller, Tyrone Tracy Jr. (> Najee), Zonovan Knight, Jaleel McLaughlin / Audric Estim\u00e9."}, {"ts": "04:30\u201306:45", "title": "04:30\u201306:45 \u00b7 Quarterbacks \u00b7 Kyler Murray (vs IND) and Aaron Rodgers (vs NO) as Wk7 starters, slight nod Rodgers; Penix (deep 1QB); Tanner McKee and J.J. McCarthy for 2QB/Superflex. Jamey's birthday break."}, {"ts": "06:45\u201308:10", "title": "06:45\u201308:10 \u00b7 Tight ends \u00b7 Hunter Henry (\"the easy one\"), Michael Mayer, Colby Parkinson vs Tyler Higbee, Tommy Tremble."}, {"ts": "08:10\u201309:59", "title": "08:10\u201309:59 \u00b7 DST \u00b7 Vikings (#1, vs IND), Browns (vs TEN), Jets over Dolphins, sneaky Cardinals (vs DEN). Adam's DST stat. Sign-off."}], "host_profiles": {"Jamey Eisenberg": {"fields": {"overall tone": ["Measured and a bit pessimistic about the wire: \"not great,\" and RBs get a flat \"No.\" Confidence comes from roles and opportunity, not from upside."], "bullish": ["Omar Cooper Jr. (4/5: \"headliner,\" a WR3 the rest of the season), Hunter Henry (5/5: \"the easy one\"), Kyler Murray (4/5: \"good upcoming stretch\"), J.J. McCarthy in 2QB/SF (5/5: \"must be picked up\"), Vikings DST (5/5: \"my number one\"), Jordan Tyson stash (4/5: \"definitely stash him\")."], "lukewarm": ["DeMario Douglas (3/5: \"wouldn't spend a lot of fab\"), Kendre Miller (2/5: \"touchdown dependent\"), Tyrone Tracy (2/5: \"I have no idea what to make of it\"), Michael Mayer (3/5: \"low-end starting option\"), Parkinson and Tremble (2/5: deeper leagues)."], "bearish": ["Najee Harris (not \"the preferred alternate plan\"), Bo Nix (as a DST target), and the RB pool overall."], "news call (confirmed by espn/ap oct 19)": ["\"Jalen Hurts is now out for the season\" and McKee is the starter \"for the foreseeable future.\""], "quotes": ["\"This receiving class, this rookie receiving class, uh, we we sort of crapped all over it a little bit.\" / \"Any good running backs to pick up this week?\" \"No.\" / \"50 is a new 30.\""]}, "text": "- **Overall 